ref_dict.prop:theBasicLemma:
\begin{proposition}\label{prop:theBasicLemma}
    Let $G$, $\mu$ and $\nu_\mu$ be as above. Let $f\colon G\lora\C$ be a measurable function such that for $\nu_\mu$-almost every trajectory $\ler{w_n}_n\in G^\N$, the values $f\ler{w_n}$ converge. Let $m$ be a fixed positive integer. Then for $\nu_\mu\times\mu^{*m}$-almost every pair $\ler{(w_n)_n,\gamma}\in G^\N\times G$, we have
