For a completeness, we will give a proof as in the appendix.

First we will have the
long-time solution of (\ref{2020C}):

\begin{theorem}
\label{T1A}Let $(M,\xi,\eta,g,\Phi,\omega)$ be a complete noncompact Sasakian
