ref_dict.def:U-small:
\begin{defn}\label{def:U-small} 
Fix a smaller neighbourhood $U\subset U_0$ such that
\begin{equation}\label{Uconditions}
 U\cdot U\subset U_0, \qquad e \in U.
\end{equation}
For $q \geq  n\ge 0$ we define a $G$-invariant subset of $G^{n+1}$ by
\begin{equation}\label{ball}
 S_{n,G,U}
 :=
 \bigl\{ (g_0,\dots,g_n)\in G^{n+1}\ \bigm|\ g_i^{-1}g_j\in U\ \text{for all }0\le i,j\le n\bigr\}.
\end{equation}
We refer elements of $S_{n,G,U}$ as to \emph{$U$-small $(n+1)$-tuples}.
\end{defn}

