	If $Y$ is an $\calO$-compact $d$-oriented prestack and $X$ an $n$-shifted Poisson derived Artin stack such that $\MapSt(Y,X)$ is locally of finite presentation. Then the mapping prestack
	\[\MapSt(Y,X)\]
	has a natural $(n-d)$-shifted Poisson structure.
\end{thmintro}

