ref_dict.thm: main thm:
\begin{lettertheorem}\label{thm: main thm}
Let $\Delta$ be a simplicial complex so that $V(\Delta)$ is countable. Suppose there exists an increasing sequence $\Delta_1 \subseteq \Delta_2 \subseteq \ldots$ of finite full subcomplexes of $\Delta$ such that $\Delta_n$ is Cohen-Macaulay and $\bigcup_{n \in \nn} \Delta_n = \Delta$. Then, the Stanley-Reisner ring $k[\Delta]$ is a flat direct limit of the Stanley-Reisner rings $k[\Delta_n]$, and hence is Cohen-Macaulay in the sense of flat direct limits. 
\end{lettertheorem}

