\begin{theorem}\label{Thm-nonlinear} 
Let $(\overline{u}, \overline{\phi})$ be as mentioned in \Cref{rem-assump-steadystate} and let $\mathcal{O}$ be any open subset of $(0, 1)$. For any $T>0$, there exists a positive number $\mu$ such that for any $(w_0,\psi_0)\in  (L^2(0,1))^2,$ with $\norm{(w_0,\psi_0)}_{L^2\times L^2}\leq \mu,$ 
