ref_dict.conj:GEM:
\begin{conjecture}[Generalised Euclid--Mullin conjecture]
\label{conj:GEM}
Let $a,m\in\N$ with $a^2\equiv1\pmod{m}$. Then
\begin{itemize}
\item[(i)] there exists $f\in\GEM(a,m)$ such that $\GEM_1(f;a,m)$ contains
every prime $p\equiv a\pmod{m}$;
\item[(ii)] for any $f\in\GEM(a,m)$, $\GEM_2(f;a,m)$ omits infinitely many
primes $p\equiv a\pmod{m}$.
\end{itemize}
\end{conjecture}

