When \(n=1\), \(Y_{m,1}\) is diffeomorphic to the boundary \(\partial W_m\) of the Akbulut-Yasui cork in \cite[Figure 1]{zbMATH05660539}.
For the case \(m=1\), \((Y_{1,n},\sigma)\) is shown in Figure \ref{Y_1,n}. 
