\alpha(\xi)=\begin{cases}
\alpha(\phi(\xi))\,r(\phi(\xi)), & \text{if }\xi\in S,\\
0, & \text{otherwise.}
\end{cases}
\]

There exists a measurable set $S\subseteq\augS$ such that $\restr{\mu}{S}$ and its pushforward $\restr{\mu}{S}^\phi$ are equivalent measures, while $\restr{\mu}{S^c}$ and its pushforward $\restr{\mu}{S^c}^\phi$ are singular. Writing
\[r\coloneqq \frac{\mathrm d\restr{\mu}{S}^\phi}{\mathrm d\restr{\mu}{S}},\]
then the kernel $\Pimh(\xi,\mathrm d\xi')=\alpha(\xi)\,\delta_{\phi(\xi)}(\mathrm d\xi')+(1-\alpha(\xi))\,\delta_{\xi}(\mathrm d\xi')$ is $\restr{\mu}{S}$-reversible provided
\[
\alpha(\xi)=\begin{cases}
\min\{1,r(\xi)\}, & \text{if }\xi\in S,\\
0, & \text{otherwise.}
\end{cases}
\]

