Necessarily $X$ is isomorphic either to a Hirzebruch surface $\mathbb F_n$ with $n\in\{0,1,2\}$, or to one of the following surfaces (for some $n\in\{0,1,2\}$):
(1) $X\cong X_{n,1}$, the $2$-blowup $\varphi_1\colon X_{n,1}\to\mathbb P^1$ of the ruling $\pi\colon\mathbb F_n\to\mathbb P^1$ with center a point $p_1\in\mathbb F_n$ not lying on any $(-2)$-curve;
