(3) $X\cong X_{n,3}$, obtained from such an $X_{n,2}$ by a further $2$-blowup $\varphi_3\colon X_{n,3}\to\mathbb P^1$ with center a point $p_3\in X_{n,2}$ lying neither on any $(-2)$-curve of $\mathbb F_n$ nor on the fiber containing $p_1$ or $p_2$.
In every case, the destabilizing foliation $\mathcal F$ is induced by the canonical fibration $X\to\mathbb P^1$.

