\begin{corollary}
\label{cor:computeepsilon}
Let $ \rho_\lambda $ be an almost everywhere unramified $ \lambda $-adic representation of a global function field $ K = \F_q(C) $ that is self-dual of weight $ w(\rho_\lambda) $ and sign $ c(\rho_\lambda) $. Then Algorithm \ref{alg:computeepsilon} outputs $ \epsilon(\rho_\lambda) \in F_\lambda^\times $ with inputs
$$ (\LL_\bullet(\rho_\lambda, T), \ D(\rho_\lambda, T), \ n(\rho_\lambda), \ 1 / q^{w(\rho_\lambda) + 1}, \ c(\rho_\lambda)). $$
\end{corollary}

