The introduction does not give a step-by-step proof of
\begin{thm}[{\cite[Theorem 8.2]{haglund-wise2012}}]\label{malnormal combination}
Let $X$ be a compact connected nonpositively cured cube complex, and let $P$ be a hyperplane in $X$ such that the following hold:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item $\pi_1X$ is hyperbolic.
    \item $P$ is an embedded $2$-sided hyperplane in $X$.
    \item $\pi_1P$ is malnormal in $\pi_1X$.
    \item Each component of $X\setminus N_o(P)$ is virtually special.
\end{enumerate}
Then $X$ is virtually special.
\end{thm}
but it does explain how later results relate to it. In particular, it says that, in establishing the main theorem, the proof is "based on \cite[Theorem~1.4]{Huang--Wise2024fintiestature}, whose argument relies on the Malnormal Special Quotient Theorem and, in particular, on the theorem above." It also emphasizes that this dependence means "In establishing the main theorem, this does not provide a new proof of the theorem above."

