To prove the main theorem, we split the argument into two cases and use the following two propositions. 

\begin{proposition}
  \label{prop:N_large}
  For \(N_{0} = \codenumber{64}\) we have
  \begin{equation*}
    \lambda_1(\mathcal{P}_{N_0}) > \lambda_1(\mathcal{P}_{N_0+1}) >
    \dots > \lambda_1(\mathcal{P}_N) > \lambda_1(\mathcal{P}_{N+1}) >
