  Let $\kappa = 0$, and let $\Omega \subset \mathbb{R}^3$ be a bounded domain with smooth boundary. Assume that \eqref{phi} holds and that $S \in C^2([0,\infty))$ satisfies condition~\eqref{S} with $\alpha > \frac{1}{3}$. Then, for any initial data $n_0$ and $u_0$ fulfilling \eqref{initial}, the problem \eqref{1} under the boundary conditions \eqref{bdry} possesses a global classical solution $(n, c, u, P)$ satisfying
\begin{equation*}
