Let $k$ be a field.  Let $\~G \to G$ be a central isogeny of semisimple algebraic groups, the kernel of which is a group $\mu$ of multiplicative type.  If $\pi_0^{\A^1}(\~G)$ is strongly $\A^1$-invariant, then so is $\pi_0^{\A^1}(G)$.
